S11 REVIEW: APPROVED

Final check of S11 at eb31559 (done 20261117T023850-seg11-today-74dbd1). Tree: claude/naadi-shared at eb31559. No code edited; LLM mocked. D1–D8 were verified at 6d06147 (20261117T022525-review11-a222db). eb31559 changes only coach/run.py, coach/suggest.py and their tests.

## What I ran
- Unit pytest (not live / not db): 865 passed. ruff check + format clean on coach/plan; mypy: no issues.
- The stack was recreated fresh after a worker restart. db tests for tests/plan, tests/coach, RLS, RLS coverage and live_check: 158 passed (includes the new overlapping-pass db test).
- Number-check probe, 34 cases (my own script):
  - Every earlier case is still dropped: twelve/triple, hundred/double, Q99/a20, XL, ９９.
  - New cases dropped as expected:
    - "twenty-five", "twenty five" and "twenty  -  five" (odd spacing) read as 25;
    - "-5" is kept as -5;
    - "one hundred and twenty" reads as 120, and is kept when 120 is a fact;
    - "1,000" reads as 1000: kept when due = 1000, dropped when due = 1;
    - "a couple" and "a pair" read as 2, "once" as 1;
    - "twenty one" reads as 21, "hundreds" as 100;
    - NBSP-joined text and "4.2" (when 42 is the fact) are handled.
  - Kept as expected:
    - fullwidth "Ｔｗｅｌｖｅ" (NFKC → 12 when 12 is a fact);
    - "Raise your score…" ("score" no longer counts);
    - "forty-two percent", "42.0", and the valid digit and word sentences.
- Overlapping passes (my own db probe): two coach_pass calls run concurrently with a slow fake gateway (1.5 s) that writes llm_usage. Result: 1 model call for the student; pass 2 noted "locked"; 1 llm row written; 0 errors.
- CI: run 44003959626 for eb31559 was still in progress at the time of this report. The previous run, 43995510789 (6d06147), had today.spec/shell.spec and db green, and its only reds were not S11 (S12b ink-sync, S09 exam scratch ink). eb31559 touches no web code.

## Defects (none blocking)
1. Low — compound numbers joined by an en or em dash, or a sign written another way, still split or lose the sign.
   Repro:
   - numbers_ok("Try Twenty–five questions.", {questions:20, correct:5, …}) → True (read as 20 and 5);
   - "minus five points" → True (read as 5);
   - "−5 points" (U+2212) → True (read as 5).
   Expected: 25 / -5, not in the facts, so dropped.
   Fix: treat – — ‒ as hyphens when joining number words. Map U+2212 and the word "minus" to a leading "-". NFKC does not map U+2212.
   Low because the counts and percents in the facts are never negative, and models rarely write number words with an en dash.
2. Low — the advisory lock is held, inside an open transaction, for the whole model call (up to the gateway timeout plus its fallbacks). That is one pool connection idle in a transaction per student. This is fine at max_users_per_run with sequential students. If the database ever sets idle_in_transaction_session_timeout below the LLM timeout, the student's write would fail (counted in errors, rules next night). Optional: take the lock, check, mark and commit, then call the model, then write in a second short transaction guarded by the llm_usage attempt row.
